\title{thermify: Efficient Agroclimatic Thermal Indices}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Computes growing degree-days (average, single and double sine, single and double triangle methods with horizontal, vertical and intermediate cutoffs), degree-hours, chilling hours, Utah model chill units and Dynamic model chill portions from daily or hourly temperatures. Monthly climatologies can be densified to daily values with a mean-preserving interpolation, natively or through the 'tempify' Python package, and then to hourly values with sine or Linvill diurnal models. Raster workflows based on 'terra' process data in blocks. Outputs based on monthly climatologies are model-based estimates, not observations.
